1001, 23500], [23501, 30000], [30001, 42701]]}, "result_digest": "00d30257d1fbb3af", "result_summary": "{\"counts\": [{\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [4302, 7000]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [7001, 10000]}, {\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [10001, 13000]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [13001, 16000]}, {\"n_events\": 2, \"window\": [16001, 19000]}, {\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [19001, 21000]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [21001, 23500]}, {\"n_events\": 2, \"window\": [23501, 30000]}, {\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [30001, 42701]}]}", "latency_ms": 3, "tokens_before": 30058, "tokens_after": 30058, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_16", "tool": "edges_between", "args": {"u": 1932, "v": 131, "window": [10001, 14800]}, "result_digest": "f371ec4b10984c0a", "result_summary": "{\"connected\": false, \"n_events_u_to_v\": 0, \"n_events_v_to_u\": 0, \"u\": 1932, \"v\": 131, \"window\": [10001, 14800]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 39698, "tokens_after": 39698, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_d7716db7", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [798, 131, 389, 972, 1877, 1932], "window": [4302, 42701], "confidence": 0.78, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "798 and 131 appear linked only through the hub 389, but 798\u2192389 exists while 389\u2192131 does not (only 131\u2192389). 131's sole in-neighbours are 972, 1877, 1932; 1877 has no in-edges, 972 only from 1439, and 1932's predecessors exclude 798 and both of its out-neighbours (45, 389). 798's four sparse events also do not precede any 1932\u2192131 contact within the 600-unit relay limit. Hence no time-respecting cascade from 798 to 131; the ignore-time connection is a hub artefact."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure around the endpoints**\n- 798 is very sparse: only 4 events, with out-edges to just {45, 389} (step_02, step_03).\n- 131 has 7 events; its *incoming* edges come only from {972, 1877, 1932} (step_02, step_04).\n\n**The apparent connection is the hub 389, but it runs the wrong way in time/direction**\n- 389 is a massive hub (170 events, 151 partners \u2014 step_09), which is exactly the confounder that makes 798 and 131 look \"connected when time is ignored\" (steps 05/06 show both in 389's star).\n- However, the only 798\u2013389 event is 798\u2192389 (step_07), and the only 389\u2013131 event is **131\u2192389**, with zero 389\u2192131 events over the whole window (step_08, step_10). So the star through 389 cannot carry influence 798 \u2192 131 in any direction-respecting way, let alone time-respecting.\n\n**No alternative in-route to 131**\n- 1877 has no in-edges at all in the window (step_12), so it cannot be an intermediate relay.\n- 972 is reachable only from 1439 (step_11); 1932 only from {435, 1440, 1450, 1747, 1887, 1916} (step_13). None of these is 798 or one of 798's two out-neighbours (45, 389), so any route would need \u22653 further hops that the neighbourhood data does not exhibit.\n- Timing is also hostile: 798's activity is confined to isolated bursts (2 events in 10001\u201313000, then 1 each after 23500 \u2014 step_14), while 131's incoming activity is scattered across 16001\u201321000 and 23501+ (step_15); the 1932\u2192131 contact does not occur in the 600-unit reachable follow-on window after 798's early burst (step_16).\n\n**Conclusion:** the static connectivity is an artefact of the high-degree hub 389; there is no direction- and time-respecting chain with \u2264600-unit gaps from 798 to 131.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_d7716db7\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 131, 389, 972, 1877, 1932],\n  \"window\": [4302, 42701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.78,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"798 and 131 appear linked only through the hub 389, but 798\u2192389 exists while 389\u2192131 does not (only 131\u2192389). 131's sole in-neighbours are 972, 1877, 1932; 1877 has no in-edges, 972 only from 1439, and 1932's predecessors exclude 798 and both of its out-neighbours (45, 389). 798's four sparse events also do not precede any 1932\u2192131 contact within the 600-unit relay limit. Hence no time-respecting cascade from 798 to 131; the ignore-time connection is a hub artefact.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 49506, "total_output_tokens": 8734, "total_tokens": 58240, "total_latency_ms": 117883, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}